---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CardDemo from '../../components/CardDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Card" description="A bordered panel that groups a title, content, and actions.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Card</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A bordered panel that groups related content. Two sizes, a flat or raised surface, and parts for a header, content,
    and a footer.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <CardDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Card usage"
      code={`import {
  Card,
  CardAction,
  CardContent,
  CardDescription,
  CardFooter,
  CardHeader,
  CardTitle,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/card";

<Card>
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle render={<h3 />}>Meadow project</CardTitle>
    <CardDescription>Spring planting plan · 12 beds</CardDescription>
    <CardAction>
      <Badge variant="success">Active</Badge>
    </CardAction>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>Three tasks are ready to review.</CardContent>
  <CardFooter>
    <Button variant="outline">Review tasks</Button>
  </CardFooter>
</Card>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>size</code> is <code>"md"</code> (the default, 16px padding and gaps, 16px title) or <code>"sm"</code>{' '}
      (12px, 14px title). Both are exposed as the
      <code>--sprout-card-spacing</code> variable for content that needs to line up with the card edges.{' '}
      <code>surface</code> is <code>"default"</code> or
      <code>"raised"</code>, which tints the panel and adds a soft shadow in light mode for settings panels that sit on
      a surface of the same color.
    </p>
    <p>
      The root and every part render a <code>div</code> and take the Base UI
      <code>render</code> prop. <code>CardTitle</code> is not a heading by default; pass{' '}
      <code>render={'{<h3 />}'}</code> to place it in the document outline. The root exposes <code>data-size</code> and{' '}
      <code>data-surface</code>, and each part has a matching <code>data-slot</code>. <code>cardVariants()</code>
      returns the root classes for other elements.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Layout</h2>
    <p>
      <code>CardHeader</code> is a grid. A <code>CardAction</code> takes a second column and spans the title and
      description rows. Add a<code>border-b</code> class to the header to divide it from the content. A{' '}
      <code>CardFooter</code> sits flush with the bottom edge with a tinted background and top border, even when it is
      wrapped in an element such as
      <code>{'<div className="mt-auto">'}</code> that pushes it down in an equal-height grid. An image placed first or
      last runs edge to edge.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Small card in a grid"
      code={`<article aria-label={task.title} className="grid min-w-0">
  <Card size="sm">
    <CardHeader>
      <Button variant="ghost" size="card-title" nativeButton={false}
        render={<a href={task.href} />}>
        <CheckSquare size={14} aria-hidden="true" />
        <span className="line-clamp-2">{task.title}</span>
      </Button>
    </CardHeader>
    <div className="mt-auto">
      <CardFooter>…</CardFooter>
    </div>
  </Card>
</article>`}
    />
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Raised settings panel"
      code={`<Card surface="raised">
  <CardContent>
    <div className="space-y-4">…list, alerts, or a StatePanel…</div>
  </CardContent>
</Card>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      A card is a plain container with no role and no focus stop. Name the region around it with <code>section</code> or{' '}
      <code>article</code> and
      <code>aria-label</code> when it stands alone, and render the title as a heading that fits the page outline. Links
      and buttons inside keep their own focus rings, and long text wraps instead of overflowing. Theme changes fade in
      120ms and stop when reduced motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Cards use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>,<code>--sprout-text</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>, and
      <code>--sprout-radius-panel</code>. The footer tints with
      <code>--sprout-hover</code>. Raised cards use
      <code>--sprout-card-raised</code> and
      <code>--sprout-card-raised-shadow</code>, defined for light and dark modes and overridable like any other Sprõut
      token.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
